From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] system, target/i386, target/arm: the syscall trap

system/syscall-trap.c: one consumer of syscall entries and returns to user
mode, keyed by (task, user sp, pc); calls held across a fault (fault and
retry at the same trap) and across an injected call (INJECT, then REWIND to
the trap with the task's registers).  The targets report syscall entry
(syscall/sysenter/int 0x80, svc) and every return to user mode while
anything is waiting.  TLB-only lookups for the consumer's reads.

Vendored sources: src/system/syscall-trap.c,
src/include/system/syscall-trap.h.
---
